cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its readings, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "As-Agreed"
abstract: "As-Agreed checks each step of a pipeline against what was agreed. Before the last step writes its result, As-Agreed compares each declared field with the agreed record. If a field of a MUST or MUST_NOT commitment changed, As-Agreed stops that step. It tells you which field changed, and at which step. The record is a file on your disk. A test gives an error if the code imports a known network module."
